---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import FastCar from "@/assets/FastCar.jpg";
import PprPlane from "@/assets/pprAirplane.png";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
---

<Layout>
  <main class="container">

    <h2>Our sites are fast</h2>
    <figure class="photo-figure">
      
      <Image
        src={FastCar}
        alt="Red sports car in motion"
        class="photo car"
        widths={[240, 360, 480, 640, 800]}
        sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 25vw, (min-width: 640px) 40vw, 80vw"
        loading="eager"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption class="caption">
        Image by <a href="https://pixabay.com/users/gkhaus-4364338/?utm_source=link-attribution&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=image&utm_content=5723726">Serhii G.</a>
        from <a href="https://pixabay.com//?utm_source=link-attribution&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=image&utm_content=5723726">Pixabay</a>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
      <section class="content-section">
        <p>Sometimes a webpage feels slow not because it’s broken, but because it’s doing too much.
        Heavy scripts, excessive client-side processing, and inefficient delivery can leave visitors staring at a loading indicator instead of your content.</p>
        <p>One factor—network quality—is outside anyone’s control. The others are not. At Titanium Hut, performance is treated as a design decision, not an afterthought.</p>
        <p>Our sites are built with restraint. Pages are delivered as clean, server-rendered HTML first,
        so content appears immediately and works even before any enhancements load. This reduces the amount of work required by the browser and keeps pages responsive across devices and connection speeds.</p>
        <p>By shipping minimal client-side JavaScript, we avoid unnecessary decoding and execution in the browser. The result is faster load times, improved accessibility, and a smoother experience for real users—not just benchmark scores. </p>
        <p>Because search engines receive clear, semantic HTML by default, your content is easier to index and understand. That clarity supports long-term SEO, accessibility, and reliability without relying on fragile client-side rendering. </p>
      </section>

    <h2>Our sites are simple</h2>
    
    <figure class="photo-figure">  
      <Image
        src={PprPlane}
        alt="Paper airplane on a solid background"
        class="photo car"
        widths={[240, 360, 480, 640, 800]}
        sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 25vw, (min-width: 640px) 40vw, 80vw"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption class="caption">
        by <a href="https://pixabay.com/users/cdd20-1193381/?utm_source=link-attribution&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=image&utm_content=5266197">Hello Cdd20</a>
        from <a href="https://pixabay.com//?utm_source=link-attribution&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=image&utm_content=5266197">Pixabay</a>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

      <p>Because pages are delivered as semantic HTML by default, search engines can clearly understand your content. That supports indexing, accessibility, and long-term SEO without relying on heavy client-side rendering.</p>

      <p>
      <button class="btn-specs" data-open-modal="#specs-modal" aria-haspopup="dialog">Check out all the specs</button></p>
  </main>

  <!-- Specs Modal -->
  <div id="specs-modal" class="modal" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal__overlay" data-close-modal></div>

    <div class="modal__dialog" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="specs-title">
      <header class="modal__header">
        <h2 id="specs-title">Everything you get</h2>
        <button class="modal__close" aria-label="Close specs" data-close-modal>&times;</button>
      </header>

      <div class="modal__body">
        <ul class="specs-list">
          <li><strong>Secure by default.</strong> Free SSL, strong security headers, and hardened forms with spam protection mean your site (and inbox) stay clean.</li>
          <li><strong>SEO that actually moves the needle.</strong> Semantic HTML, server-rendered pages, Open Graph/Twitter cards, and optional Schema.org markup help Google understand—and rank—your content.</li>
          <li><strong>Core Web Vitals, not just “fast.”</strong> We tune images, fonts, caching, and JavaScript so you pass Google’s Web Vitals (LCP, CLS, INP)—the metrics that matter for search and conversions.</li>
          <li><strong>Accessible to everyone.</strong> WCAG-focused color contrast, keyboard navigation, descriptive alt text, and skip links. Good for users, good for SEO, good for business.</li>
          <li><strong>Mobile-first experience.</strong> Looks and works perfectly on phones and tablets (most traffic is mobile).</li>
          <li><strong>Content you can update yourself.</strong> Choose what fits you: edit Markdown, Google Docs → site, or a simple headless CMS. No lock-in.</li>
          <li><strong>Rock-solid reliability.</strong> Monitoring, error alerts, and automated off-site backups so you can roll back if anything goes sideways.</li>
          <li><strong>Forms that deliver.</strong> Proper SPF/DKIM, honeypots/hCaptcha, and delivery monitoring so inquiries land in your inbox (not spam).</li>
          <li><strong>Local SEO package (optional).</strong> Google Business Profile setup, review links, NAP consistency, and LocalBusiness schema to show up in local searches/maps.</li>
          <li><strong>Integrations that save time.</strong> Booking (Calendly/SimplePractice), payments (Stripe), and chat (Crisp/Intercom) as needed—with privacy in mind.</li>
          <li><strong>Transparent care plans.</strong> Updates, backups, uptime checks, and a real person to call. Flat monthly options.</li>
          <li><strong>Brand-flexible theming.</strong> Your palette switcher lets us spin up a consistent look per client without reinventing the site.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <footer class="modal__footer">
        <button class="modal__cta" data-close-modal>Sounds good</button>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script is:inline>
    (function(){
      // Ensure closed on load unless explicitly opened
      const modalEl = document.getElementById('specs-modal');
      if (modalEl && modalEl.getAttribute('aria-hidden') !== 'false') {
        modalEl.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
      }

      const FOCUSABLE = 'a[href], area[href], input:not([disabled]), select:not([disabled]), textarea:not([disabled]), button:not([disabled]), [tabindex]:not([tabindex="-1"])';
      const openers = document.querySelectorAll('[data-open-modal]');
      let activeModal = null, lastFocused = null;

      function openModal(modal){
        if (!modal) return;
        lastFocused = document.activeElement;
        activeModal = modal;
        modal.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'false');
        document.documentElement.style.overflow = 'hidden';
        const focusables = modal.querySelectorAll(FOCUSABLE);
        (focusables[0] || modal).focus();
      }
      function closeModal(){
        if (!activeModal) return;
        activeModal.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
        document.documentElement.style.overflow = '';
        if (lastFocused) lastFocused.focus();
        activeModal = null;
      }

      openers.forEach(btn=>{
        btn.addEventListener('click', ()=>{
          const sel = btn.getAttribute('data-open-modal');
          openModal(document.querySelector(sel));
        });
      });

      document.addEventListener('click', (e)=>{
        if (e.target.closest('[data-close-modal]')) { closeModal(); }
      });

      document.addEventListener('keydown', (e)=>{
        if (!activeModal) return;
        if (e.key === 'Escape') { e.preventDefault(); closeModal(); return; }
        if (e.key === 'Tab') {
          const nodes = [...activeModal.querySelectorAll(FOCUSABLE)];
          if (nodes.length === 0) return;
          const first = nodes[0], last = nodes[nodes.length - 1];
          if (e.shiftKey && document.activeElement === first) { e.preventDefault(); last.focus(); }
          else if (!e.shiftKey && document.activeElement === last) { e.preventDefault(); first.focus(); }
        }
      });
    })();
  </script>

  <style>
    /* ====== Modal trigger button ====== */
    .btn-specs {
      background: var(--cta, #852E2F);
      color: var(--bg, #fff);
      border: 0;
      padding: .7rem 1rem;
      border-radius: .75rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      cursor: pointer;
      box-shadow: 0 6px 16px rgba(0,0,0,.12);
    }
    .btn-specs:hover { background: var(--cta-dark, #652024); }

    /* ====== ID-scoped modal: hidden by default ====== */
    #specs-modal {
      display: none;                 /* hide by default */
      position: fixed;
      inset: 0;
      z-index: 9999;
    }
    #specs-modal[aria-hidden="false"] {
      display: block;                /* show when opened */
    }

    /* Overlay & dialog */
    #specs-modal .modal__overlay {
      position: absolute; inset: 0;
      background: rgba(0,0,0,.45);
      backdrop-filter: blur(2px);
    }
    #specs-modal .modal__dialog {
      position: relative; z-index: 1;
      max-width: min(900px, 92vw);
      margin: 6vh auto;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--brand) 0%, var(--cta) 100%);
      color: #fff;
      border-radius: 1rem;
      box-shadow: 0 20px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.35);
      overflow: hidden;
      transform: translateY(8px);
      animation: modal-in 180ms ease-out both;
    }

    .container{
  color: antiquewhite;
  line-height: 1.6;
  text-size-adjust: 100%;
  max-width: 70ch;
  margin: 2rem auto;
  padding: 0 1rem;
}


    #specs-modal .modal__header {
      display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;
      padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18);
      background: transparent;
    }
    #specs-modal .modal__header h2 { margin: 0; font-size: 1.35rem; color: #fff; }

    #specs-modal .modal__close {
      appearance: none; background: transparent; border: 0; cursor: pointer;
      font-size: 1.6rem; line-height: 1; color: #fff; opacity: .9;
    }
    #specs-modal .modal__close:hover { opacity: 1; }

    #specs-modal .modal__body {
      padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem 0;
      max-height: 60vh; overflow: auto;
      color: #fff;
      font-size: 1.075rem;
      line-height: 1.65;
    }
    #specs-modal .specs-list { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; }
    #specs-modal .specs-list li { margin: 0 0 .85rem; }
    #specs-modal .specs-list li strong { color: #fff; font-weight: 700; }
    #specs-modal .modal__body a {
      color: #fff;
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 2px;
    }

    #specs-modal .modal__footer {
      display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; gap: .5rem;
      padding: 1rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18);
    }
    #specs-modal .modal__cta {
      background: transparent;
      color: #fff;
      border: 1.6px solid rgba(255,255,255,.7);
      padding: .6rem 1rem; border-radius: .6rem; cursor: pointer;
    }
    #specs-modal .modal__cta:hover { border-color: #fff; filter: brightness(1.08); }

    @keyframes modal-in {
      from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(16px); }
      to   { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
    }

    /* ====== Images & captions centered ====== */
    /* ====== Images & captions centered ====== */
.photo-figure { margin: 1.5rem auto; text-align: center; }

.caption {
  font-size: 0.95rem;
  margin: .5rem auto 0;
  text-align: center;
  max-width: 40rem;
  color: aliceblue;
}

.caption a:link,
.caption a:visited {
  color: aliceblue;
  text-decoration-color: currentColor;
}

.caption a:hover,
.caption a:focus-visible {
  color: #F7F2EB;
  text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
  text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
}


    .photo.car {
      display: block;
      width: 25%;
      height: auto;
      margin: 0 auto;
      border-radius: 1rem;
    }
    @media (max-width: 768px) { .photo.car { width: 60%; } }

    
  </style>
</Layout>
